{"name":"White Pepper","hex":"#ae9e86","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white pepper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spice consisting of the light-colored seed of the black pepper fruit without the dark-colored pulp and skin. Used as a spice in light colored foods such as cream sauces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white_pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"White Pepper","blocks":[{"text":"White Pepper is the seventh studio album by the American rock band Ween, and the last album they released on Elektra Records. It was released on May 2, 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1e/Ween-WhitePepper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Pepper"},{"title":"Black pepper","blocks":[{"text":"Black pepper is a flowering vine in the family Piperaceae, cultivated for its fruit, which is usually dried and used as a spice and seasoning. The fruit is a drupe (stonefruit) which is about 5 mm in diameter, dark red, and contains a stone which encloses a single pepper seed. Peppercorns and the ground pepper derived from them may be described simply as pepper, or more precisely as black pepper, green pepper, or white pepper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Piper_nigrum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-107.jpg/330px-Piper_nigrum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-107.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_pepper"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/1280px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black pepper vine climbing on jackfruit tree (Artocarpus heterophyllus)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/1280px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Single stem with flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%